1246
01:01:10,291 --> 01:01:11,917
Now, what is your new number?

1247
01:01:12,627 --> 01:01:16,963
$70,562 now in my account.

1248
01:01:17,131 --> 01:01:18,506
(CHEERING)

1249
01:01:20,259 --> 01:01:25,805
Is it possible that Josepha's balance went up
the exact amount that Art's went down?

1250
01:01:26,140 --> 01:01:28,642
Hey. Check it out. It's happening again.

1251
01:01:28,809 --> 01:01:29,851
DANIEL: Is it?

1252
01:01:31,145 --> 01:01:33,480
HENLEY: Wow. It is.

1253
01:01:33,814 --> 01:01:36,983
Art's balance has gone down another 280K.

1254
01:01:37,151 --> 01:01:39,194
Dina Robertson? What did yours say?

1255
01:01:39,445 --> 01:01:43,198
$281,477.

1256
01:01:43,616 --> 01:01:44,866
(CHEERING)

1257
01:01:47,161 --> 01:01:48,828
We have a confession to make.

1258
01:01:49,038 --> 01:01:51,039
She's right. We lied about something.

1259
01:01:51,123 --> 01:01:52,791
Yes. None of you were chosen at random.

1260
01:01:52,917 --> 01:01:55,335
All of you have one thing in common.

1261
01:01:55,878 --> 01:01:57,796
Everyone in this room was a victim

1262
01:01:57,880 --> 01:02:00,674
of the hard times that hit one of
America's most treasured cities.

1263
01:02:00,758 --> 01:02:03,343
Some of you lost your houses, your cars.

1264
01:02:03,844 --> 01:02:05,887
- Your businesses.
- Your loved ones.

1265
01:02:06,013 --> 01:02:09,182
But all of you were insured
by the same company.

1266
01:02:09,350 --> 01:02:10,976
ALL: Tressler Insurance.

1267
01:02:12,520 --> 01:02:13,520
MERRITT: You were abandoned.

1268
01:02:13,604 --> 01:02:14,688
You were loopholed...

1269
01:02:14,772 --> 01:02:15,981
...out of your settlements.

1270
01:02:17,358 --> 01:02:19,985
This is all for show. Correct?

1271
01:02:20,194 --> 01:02:21,444
"All" meaning we're doing it onstage

1272
01:02:21,529 --> 01:02:22,737
in front of a paying audience?

1273
01:02:22,905 --> 01:02:24,531
- Then, yes, it's for show.
- MAN: Whoa! Whoa!

1274
01:02:24,824 --> 01:02:27,325
I've got $82,000 in my bank account!

1275
01:02:27,493 --> 01:02:29,327
It says it right here on my cell phone!

1276
01:02:29,578 --> 01:02:32,539
Everybody, look at your cell phones
right now! Everybody!

1277
01:02:32,707 --> 01:02:33,707
(CELL PHONES CHIMING)

1278
01:02:34,417 --> 01:02:35,834
(ALL CHEERING)

1279
01:02:39,130 --> 01:02:40,213
Whoo!

1280
01:02:40,506 --> 01:02:41,506
Is this for real?

1281
01:02:41,716 --> 01:02:42,882
I don't know.

1282
01:02:43,175 --> 01:02:44,259
DYLAN: Is this happening?

1283
01:02:44,427 --> 01:02:46,011
I don't know! I can't tell!

1284
01:02:46,762 --> 01:02:48,888
Hey! Did you do this?

1285
01:02:50,099 --> 01:02:51,349
JACK: How could we, Art?

1286
01:02:51,559 --> 01:02:52,726
We don't have your password.

1287
01:02:52,893 --> 01:02:56,187
We'd need access to information
we could never get our hands on.

1288
01:02:56,397 --> 01:03:00,108
Ah, yes, security questions, for instance, like,
I don't know, your mother's maiden name

1289
01:03:00,234 --> 01:03:01,776
or the name of your first pet.

1290
01:03:01,902 --> 01:03:03,695
Where would we get that information, Art?

1291
01:03:04,071 --> 01:03:05,697
You certainly would never tell us.

1292
01:03:08,492 --> 01:03:10,702
FULLER: We got confirmation.
It's really happening. They robbed him.

1293
01:03:12,913 --> 01:03:14,372
Do not let them get away.

1294
01:03:14,457 --> 01:03:16,458
Hey, we left you the jet and the Rolls.

1295
01:03:21,714 --> 01:03:23,048
(SHOUTING ANGRILY)

1296
01:03:23,424 --> 01:03:24,758
You got hell to pay!

1297
01:03:27,762 --> 01:03:28,762
DYLAN: Stop!

1298
01:03:29,472 --> 01:03:31,264
Stop! Nobody move!

1299
01:03:33,225 --> 01:03:34,309
Freeze!

1300
01:03:34,560 --> 01:03:36,102
Quarterback!

1301
01:03:38,981 --> 01:03:41,399
ALL: We are The Four Horsemen.

1302
01:03:41,484 --> 01:03:42,525
Good night.

1303
01:03:42,610 --> 01:03:43,735
(GRUNTING)

1304
01:03:54,789 --> 01:03:56,164
DYLAN: Get 'em off me!

1305
01:03:56,916 --> 01:03:58,500
Get off! Get off me!

1306
01:04:06,342 --> 01:04:07,342
(SIRENS WAILING)

1307
01:04:08,886 --> 01:04:10,303
Get off me!

1308
01:04:18,604 --> 01:04:20,772
All right. I want everyone
on the street! Everyone!

1309
01:04:25,903 --> 01:04:26,986
(THADDEUS CHUCKLING)

1310
01:04:27,696 --> 01:04:29,531
ALL: Quarterback!

1311
01:04:31,075 --> 01:04:33,827
Fuller, meet me in front of the theater
and bring the tracker.

1312
01:04:34,370 --> 01:04:36,663
Let's go! Let's go! Now! Come on! Let's go!

1313
01:04:36,831 --> 01:04:37,914
Give me the tracker.

1314
01:04:38,374 --> 01:04:39,374
Let's go.

1315
01:04:43,587 --> 01:04:44,712
FBl! Clear!

1316
01:04:45,422 --> 01:04:46,422
- Dylan!
- DYLAN: Damn.

1317
01:04:46,715 --> 01:04:47,674
What have you got?

1318
01:04:47,758 --> 01:04:49,342
That's him right there. Follow the red dot.

1319
01:04:49,426 --> 01:04:52,470
All right, I'll take this.
Go. Box 'em. Cut 'em off that way.

1320
01:04:54,390 --> 01:04:55,890
He's turning left on Burgundy.

1321
01:05:10,573 --> 01:05:12,031
(CAR ALARMS BLARING)

1322
01:05:17,872 --> 01:05:18,872
(GRUNTS)

1323
01:05:19,540 --> 01:05:21,082
- DYLAN: Oh!
- (CRASHING)

1324
01:05:25,963 --> 01:05:27,422
(TRACKER BEEPING)

1325
01:05:32,970 --> 01:05:34,262
Hey! Move!

1326
01:05:34,597 --> 01:05:35,930
- Move! Move!
- Oh!

1327
01:05:36,223 --> 01:05:37,807
(ALL CLAMORING)

1328
01:05:38,559 --> 01:05:40,101
I got him heading north on Bourbon.

1329
01:05:40,477 --> 01:05:42,187
- Sorry. Move, move!
- Hey!

1330
01:05:42,271 --> 01:05:44,063
Hey, excuse me. Move, move! Excuse me.

1331
01:05:45,774 --> 01:05:46,816
Ow!

1332
01:05:55,534 --> 01:05:57,202
I've lost him at Bourbon.

1333
01:06:02,583 --> 01:06:03,958
Damn! Where are you?

1334
01:06:16,472 --> 01:06:17,680
Excuse me.

1335
01:06:23,979 --> 01:06:25,605
He's heading south on Exchange Place.

1336
01:06:28,150 --> 01:06:29,192
Stop!

1337
01:06:36,200 --> 01:06:37,408
What are you doing?

1338
01:06:40,996 --> 01:06:42,413
DYLAN: He's going in Napoleon House.

1339
01:06:42,498 --> 01:06:43,623
(SIREN WAILS)

1340
01:06:45,250 --> 01:06:47,210
- Move! Move!
- (WOMAN SCREAMS)

1341
01:06:47,670 --> 01:06:49,212
Move out of the way!

1342
01:06:49,880 --> 01:06:50,880
Hey!

1343
01:06:51,715 --> 01:06:52,715
Move!

1344
01:06:55,010 --> 01:06:57,261
He's in the bathroom.
I have him in the bathroom.

1345
01:06:57,388 --> 01:06:59,681
(GRUNTS) No! No! No!

1346
01:07:01,558 --> 01:07:02,725
AGENTS: Freeze!

1347
01:07:03,560 --> 01:07:05,019
- FULLER: Lower your weapons!
- (DEVICES BEEPING)

1348
01:07:05,104 --> 01:07:08,439
What? I'm tracking myself!

1349
01:07:08,941 --> 01:07:10,900
NEWSCASTER: The Horsemen
left egg on the face of what they call

1350
01:07:10,985 --> 01:07:16,280
the alphabet agencies, calling into question
the efficacy of the FBI's task force

1351
01:07:16,532 --> 01:07:19,033
as well as the man in charge
of the investigation,

1352
01:07:19,118 --> 01:07:22,620
Special Agent Dylan Rhodes,
who was publicly ridiculed,

1353
01:07:22,705 --> 01:07:25,581
and even tackled at tonight's performance.

1354
01:07:25,916 --> 01:07:27,208
Talk about a fumble.

1355
01:07:27,418 --> 01:07:29,252
This is quickly becoming a national story,

1356
01:07:29,336 --> 01:07:32,130
as The Horsemen have now seemingly
pulled off the impossible

1357
01:07:32,214 --> 01:07:34,507
for the second time in as many days.

1358
01:07:34,925 --> 01:07:38,094
Two nights ago in Vegas, The Horsemen
seemingly robbed a bank in Paris...

1359
01:07:38,262 --> 01:07:39,429
Hey.

1360
01:07:40,723 --> 01:07:43,266
- What are you doing?
- I'm having a drink.

1361
01:07:46,437 --> 01:07:47,770
I came to get you.

1362
01:07:48,230 --> 01:07:49,230
I'm worried about you.

1363
01:07:49,314 --> 01:07:51,149
You're worried about me.
Well, I'm worried about you.

1364
01:07:51,233 --> 01:07:53,693
- Atlas. You had him.
- He didn't have a weapon.

1365
01:07:53,777 --> 01:07:55,069
I couldn't shoot him and you know that.

1366
01:07:55,154 --> 01:07:57,989
Yeah, but you... You let him go.

1367
01:07:58,407 --> 01:07:59,615
Didn't you?

1368
01:08:00,409 --> 01:08:03,202
A pretty French girl shows up out of the blue,
acts like she's my partner

1369
01:08:03,287 --> 01:08:04,996
- and then she lets the bad guy go?
- Let go of my arm.

1370
01:08:05,080 --> 01:08:06,748
Who exactly are you anyway?

1371
01:08:07,750 --> 01:08:08,833
(GRUNTS)

1372
01:08:09,001 --> 01:08:11,002
I thought you said you were a desk agent.

1373
01:08:15,841 --> 01:08:17,091
Not bad.

1374
01:08:19,094 --> 01:08:20,094
What is this?

1375
01:08:23,140 --> 01:08:24,599
What's the Eye of Horus?

1376
01:08:24,808 --> 01:08:27,894
Oh, certainly nothing
I want to get into tonight.

1377
01:08:27,978 --> 01:08:30,521
You're dismissive enough
about me when you're sober.

1378
01:08:30,814 --> 01:08:32,690
Find your way back yourself.

1379
01:08:36,987 --> 01:08:40,198
Mr. Bradley? Mr. Tressler would like you
to join him for a drink.

1380
01:08:49,583 --> 01:08:50,625
Sir.

1381
01:08:50,834 --> 01:08:51,876
TRESSLER: Thank you.

1382
01:08:53,462 --> 01:08:55,671
What is your role with them?

1383
01:08:55,839 --> 01:08:56,839
Role?

1384
01:08:57,049 --> 01:08:58,758
Yes. You seem to know
everything about them.

1385
01:08:58,842 --> 01:09:00,760
What they're gonna do.
Where they're gonna be.

1386
01:09:00,844 --> 01:09:04,055
If it makes you feel any better,
this wasn't about you.

1387
01:09:04,139 --> 01:09:07,600
Please tell me why this was not about me.

1388
01:09:08,143 --> 01:09:10,728
This is a magic trick, Mr. Tressler.

1389
01:09:10,979 --> 01:09:13,314
Played out on a global scale.

1390
01:09:13,690 --> 01:09:17,652
You, sir, are the abracadabra.

1391
01:09:18,195 --> 01:09:20,988
The distraction,
while they set up the real trick.

1392
01:09:21,198 --> 01:09:25,368
I was a $140-million distraction?

1393
01:09:26,203 --> 01:09:27,370
Yes.

1394
01:09:28,038 --> 01:09:32,208
And that very ego that got you involved
with them in the first place

1395
01:09:32,668 --> 01:09:34,210
is what keeps you from seeing that.

1396
01:09:34,336 --> 01:09:35,628
- You know...
- "I can destroy you. "

1397
01:09:35,712 --> 01:09:37,380
Yes, I do know.

1398
01:09:37,589 --> 01:09:38,881
Well, you won't.

1399
01:09:39,424 --> 01:09:41,592
And you won't destroy them.

1400
01:09:42,052 --> 01:09:46,848
Whatever this grand trick is,
it was designed a long time ago.

1401
01:09:47,057 --> 01:09:51,602
And I believe that what's about to follow
is really going to amaze.

1402
01:09:52,437 --> 01:09:56,983
So I suggest you sit back
and enjoy your front row seat.

1403
01:09:57,442 --> 01:10:00,111
You paid quite a lot of good money for it.

1404
01:10:00,320 --> 01:10:02,363
Whatever you stand to make...

1405
01:10:04,491 --> 01:10:08,035
I'll double it, if you expose them now.

1406
01:10:08,245 --> 01:10:09,579
And destroy them.

1407
01:10:10,038 --> 01:10:12,039
I stand to make five million.

1408
01:10:12,749 --> 01:10:14,000
Am I flinching?

1409
01:10:16,128 --> 01:10:17,712
No, you're not.

1410
01:11:38,627 --> 01:11:39,752
Hey.

1411
01:11:41,129 --> 01:11:43,297
I'm sorry for your arm.

1412
01:11:43,382 --> 01:11:44,966
No. I'm sorry.

1413
01:11:45,050 --> 01:11:47,301
I was an asshole. I was drunk.

1414
01:11:49,304 --> 01:11:51,889
I'm at a loss.

1415
01:11:53,809 --> 01:11:59,230
You know, when Merritt said I hardly spent
any time away from the desk, he was right.

1416
01:11:59,314 --> 01:12:02,608
I'm a researcher. That's what I do best.

1417
01:12:03,694 --> 01:12:07,613
So what's this all about?

1418
01:12:08,323 --> 01:12:10,950
Supposedly, if you buy into it,

1419
01:12:11,034 --> 01:12:13,703
The Eye are the keepers of real magic

1420
01:12:13,787 --> 01:12:16,664
and the protectors of those who practice it.

1421
01:12:16,748 --> 01:12:18,708
"Candidates for initiations

1422
01:12:18,792 --> 01:12:21,919
"must follow a series of commands
with blind obedience. "

1423
01:12:22,963 --> 01:12:26,173
- This isn't real.
- But there are some who think it is.

1424
01:12:26,591 --> 01:12:28,175
May I?

1425
01:12:29,970 --> 01:12:34,015
According to this,
they only take new people twice a century.

1426
01:12:34,349 --> 01:12:37,768
So what? The Horsemen are doing
these shows in order to get into this thing?

1427
01:12:37,853 --> 01:12:39,061
- I don't know.
- I don't know.

1428
01:12:39,146 --> 01:12:44,150
I mean, I guess these guys
could just rob banks to rob banks.

1429
01:12:44,234 --> 01:12:46,569
They don't have to put on a show for that.

1430
01:12:46,653 --> 01:12:48,154
It's probably just a myth.

1431
01:12:48,238 --> 01:12:52,241
But it doesn't make any sense,
and I don't think logic will solve this for us.

1432
01:12:52,326 --> 01:12:54,910
- You don't say?
- No.

1433
01:12:56,288 --> 01:13:00,916
I believe that some things are only discovered

1434
01:13:01,001 --> 01:13:05,379
if you take certain leaps.

1435
01:13:12,387 --> 01:13:13,888
Well, I gotta get to...

1436
01:13:14,056 --> 01:13:15,514
Yeah. Yeah.

1437
01:13:15,599 --> 01:13:17,767
- Thanks. Good night.
- Yeah. Good night.

1438
01:13:17,851 --> 01:13:19,643
- Sorry.
- It's all right.

1439
01:13:22,147 --> 01:13:24,482
If The Eye did exist, we'd have to assume
they were watching us, right?

1440
01:13:24,566 --> 01:13:25,566
(PHONE BEEPING)

1441
01:13:25,734 --> 01:13:26,942
Shit.

1442
01:13:27,027 --> 01:13:29,653
I think someone is watching us,
but it isn't magic.

1443
01:13:29,738 --> 01:13:32,698
Your fears are correct.
This is not and has never been your phone.

1444
01:13:32,783 --> 01:13:37,495
It's a clone in every way, except for this.

1445
01:13:37,579 --> 01:13:38,871
A bug.

1446
01:13:38,955 --> 01:13:42,792
Someone has heard every call, read every text.

1447
01:13:42,959 --> 01:13:44,210
That's how they were able to stay ahead of us.

1448
01:13:44,294 --> 01:13:45,086
God damn it!

1449
01:13:46,588 --> 01:13:48,339
Get me Atlas' interrogation tape.

1450
01:13:48,590 --> 01:13:50,841
Yes, sir. I have it on the hard drive.

1451
01:13:51,968 --> 01:13:53,052
Picture's up.

1452
01:13:53,512 --> 01:13:55,262
DYLAN: Okay, fast forward.

1453
01:13:55,639 --> 01:13:57,098
Go on, go on. Freeze!

1454
01:13:57,891 --> 01:13:59,683
Okay. Frame by frame. Go on.

1455
01:14:00,560 --> 01:14:01,602
Play it through.

1456
01:14:02,729 --> 01:14:05,022
Ah! Stop. Zoom in tighter. Tighter.

1457
01:14:05,482 --> 01:14:07,274
There. That's where he took my phone.

1458
01:14:08,568 --> 01:14:09,860
Is that thing transmitting?

1459
01:14:09,945 --> 01:14:11,362
Only when you're making a call
or sending a text.

1460
01:14:11,530 --> 01:14:12,488
Plus I removed the bug.

1461
01:14:12,572 --> 01:14:14,115
All right. Put it back in and turn on the phone.

1462
01:14:14,366 --> 01:14:16,158
They don't know that we know about the bug.

1463
01:14:16,368 --> 01:14:18,369
As of this instant, we are ahead of them.

1464
01:14:18,453 --> 01:14:20,538
We need to keep it that way. Understand?

1465
01:14:20,997 --> 01:14:22,289
Find my real phone and track it.

1466
01:14:22,374 --> 01:14:25,418
Already did. As of about 20 minutes ago,
it's in New York City.

1467
01:14:25,961 --> 01:14:27,002
Good.

1468
01:14:27,379 --> 01:14:30,172
I wanna cut 'em off at the knees.
They got power? Cut it.

1469
01:14:30,465 --> 01:14:33,759
They got phones, electricity, water? Cut it.

1470
01:14:33,969 --> 01:14:36,720
Squeeze 'em out.
I want 'em to feel our presence.

1471
01:14:36,930 --> 01:14:38,389
And get me an airplane!

1472
01:14:41,184 --> 01:14:42,268
The firewall's down.

1473
01:14:42,352 --> 01:14:43,811
- Do they know about this?
- DANIEL: They who?

1474
01:14:43,895 --> 01:14:45,813
"They," "them," whoever we're working for.

1475
01:14:45,897 --> 01:14:49,525
Who are we working for?
And are we prepared to go to jail for them?

1476
01:14:49,609 --> 01:14:51,819
- DANIEL: Stop being paranoid.
- It really does happen.

1477
01:14:51,903 --> 01:14:53,737
It happened to you.
Doesn't mean it's gonna happen to us.

1478
01:14:53,822 --> 01:14:55,406
Guys, I don't know if can do this, all right.

1479
01:14:55,490 --> 01:14:56,782
I don't want to go to jail, you know?

1480
01:14:56,867 --> 01:14:58,659
Then don't screw up.
You're always talking about wanting

1481
01:14:58,743 --> 01:14:59,743
to be treated like an adult.

1482
01:14:59,828 --> 01:15:01,203
Now might be a good time
to start acting like one.

1483
01:15:01,288 --> 01:15:03,414
Stick to the plan. Stay here and burn it all.

1484
01:15:06,626 --> 01:15:07,877
(TIRES SCREECHING)

1485
01:15:16,553 --> 01:15:17,678
MERRITT: I don't know what I'm doing here.

1486
01:15:17,762 --> 01:15:18,846
I don't know what you would do
anywhere else.

1487
01:15:18,930 --> 01:15:21,724
I'm here for the pot of gold
at the end of the rainbow.

1488
01:15:21,808 --> 01:15:23,851
That's it. Then I'm gone.

1489
01:15:23,935 --> 01:15:26,312
You can do whatever you want
when this is over, Merritt.

1490
01:15:26,396 --> 01:15:28,355
But until then, you stick to the plan.

1491
01:15:28,440 --> 01:15:30,566
Hey, guys. Uh... They're here.

1492
01:15:32,486 --> 01:15:34,361
- My guys are ready to go.
- Let's do this quickly...

1493
01:15:34,571 --> 01:15:35,779
- Uh. No.
- What?

1494
01:15:35,864 --> 01:15:37,323
She doesn't have jurisdiction here.

1495
01:15:37,407 --> 01:15:38,616
She's Interpol. She's with me.

1496
01:15:38,700 --> 01:15:40,910
- She stays.
- What? What?

1497
01:15:41,203 --> 01:15:42,203
Stay in the car.

1498
01:15:44,456 --> 01:15:45,664
Let's go.

1499
01:15:51,463 --> 01:15:52,505
MERRITT: Okay. Let's do it.

1500
01:15:56,801 --> 01:15:57,801
FBl!

1501
01:16:02,057 --> 01:16:03,390
MERRITT: Ladies first.

1502
01:16:03,975 --> 01:16:05,267
- Don't move!
- (SCREAMING)

1503
01:16:10,774 --> 01:16:12,691
- (CELL PHONE RINGING)
- Tell me.

1504
01:16:12,776 --> 01:16:14,360
Is my money being well-spent?

1505
01:16:15,028 --> 01:16:16,904
- Exceedingly well.
- (CAMERA CLICKING)

1506
01:16:18,698 --> 01:16:20,199
Now you tell me,

1507
01:16:20,992 --> 01:16:22,326
how do you like your Horsemen?

1508
01:16:22,410 --> 01:16:24,787
Fricasseed or fried?

1509
01:16:24,871 --> 01:16:25,913
Shredded.

1510
01:16:27,249 --> 01:16:28,707
I'll tell the chef.

1511
01:17:34,316 --> 01:17:35,691
(GRUNTING)

1512
01:17:38,486 --> 01:17:39,820
(DISPOSAL WHIRRING)

1513
01:17:44,284 --> 01:17:45,284
Freeze!

1514
01:17:52,500 --> 01:17:53,626
- Dylan!
- (WHIRRING)

1515
01:17:54,419 --> 01:17:55,586
DYLAN: Hold on!

1516
01:17:57,922 --> 01:17:58,964
Oh, you little...

1517
01:18:03,470 --> 01:18:04,470
Come here!

1518
01:18:06,222 --> 01:18:08,140
OFFICER: Five is clear. Standing by for six.

1519
01:18:08,475 --> 01:18:10,351
- You little shit!
- (IMITATING) You little shit!

1520
01:18:10,602 --> 01:18:12,728
- What game are you playing?
- What game are you playing?

1521
01:18:13,229 --> 01:18:15,147
We're all good at six. Move to seven.

1522
01:18:15,231 --> 01:18:17,274
Copy that. Going to seven. Go, go, go!

1523
01:18:18,193 --> 01:18:19,860
No, no, no, no, no. Go back!

1524
01:18:20,737 --> 01:18:21,862
Hey!

1525
01:18:23,615 --> 01:18:24,865
DYLAN: Come here!

1526
01:18:28,244 --> 01:18:29,411
(GRUNTING)

1527
01:18:32,082 --> 01:18:33,290
Ah!

1528
01:18:55,897 --> 01:18:57,022
Come here!

1529
01:18:57,107 --> 01:18:58,816
All right, whoa, hold on, hold on!

1530
01:19:00,735 --> 01:19:02,569
- Really?
- Yup.

1531
01:19:03,071 --> 01:19:04,071
Ow!

1532
01:19:06,741 --> 01:19:07,741
Oh, you...

1533
01:19:09,119 --> 01:19:10,119
Ow!

1534
01:19:11,162 --> 01:19:12,621
You little... (YELLING)

1535
01:19:18,837 --> 01:19:19,837
(GRUNTS)

1536
01:19:29,055 --> 01:19:30,097
Shit!

1537
01:19:36,813 --> 01:19:37,938
(DYLAN YELLING)

1538
01:19:48,491 --> 01:19:49,533
Shit!

1539
01:19:49,617 --> 01:19:50,784
(PANTING)

1540
01:19:50,952 --> 01:19:51,952
Give me that!

1541
01:19:52,203 --> 01:19:53,245
(GROANS)

1542
01:20:16,019 --> 01:20:17,269
(CAR LOCK CHIRPS)

1543
01:20:18,188 --> 01:20:19,772
FULLER: All units, cover the north exit now!

1544
01:20:19,856 --> 01:20:20,939
Clear on Evan.

1545
01:20:21,483 --> 01:20:23,025
FULLER: Block every possible exit.

1546
01:20:23,151 --> 01:20:24,276
Hey! Get back... Shit.

1547
01:20:26,029 --> 01:20:28,155
- FBl. Sort of. I need your car. Thanks.
- What?

1548
01:20:28,239 --> 01:20:29,239
What?

1549
01:20:30,658 --> 01:20:32,993
- Elvis, help me out, bud.
- Thank you very much.

1550
01:20:33,203 --> 01:20:35,621
In Jack's bowl
are ping pong balls with section numbers.

1551
01:20:35,830 --> 01:20:37,831
Jack, could you hand me a section number?

1552
01:20:38,041 --> 01:20:39,416
Thank you. We are looking at Section B.

1553
01:20:39,626 --> 01:20:41,376
- Where is Section B?
- (CHEERING)

1554
01:20:41,461 --> 01:20:43,921
Okay. There.
It's gonna be one of you guys. Get ready.

1555
01:20:44,422 --> 01:20:45,756
I don't know why everybody's happy.

1556
01:20:45,840 --> 01:20:46,882
It's only them.

1557
01:20:47,175 --> 01:20:48,509
Merritt, can I get a row, please?

1558
01:20:50,929 --> 01:20:52,554
Stop! Stop!

1559
01:21:00,897 --> 01:21:01,980
(GRUNTS)

1560
01:21:08,696 --> 01:21:09,738
Hey!

1561
01:21:12,075 --> 01:21:14,493
- (GROANING)
- (HANDCUFFS CLICKING)

1562
01:21:39,519 --> 01:21:40,519
Good. Follow him!

1563
01:21:40,603 --> 01:21:42,688
Don't ever tell me to stay in the car. Ever.

1564
01:21:42,772 --> 01:21:44,106
I didn't have tactical command.

1565
01:21:44,190 --> 01:21:46,525
If you don't trust me, just tell me.

1566
01:21:46,609 --> 01:21:48,193
Promise me, next time, you will back me up.

1567
01:21:48,278 --> 01:21:50,362
Could we have
this conversation later, please?

1568
01:21:50,446 --> 01:21:52,030
No!

1569
01:21:52,115 --> 01:21:54,324
Okay, fine, I promise. Now, go!

1570
01:21:56,619 --> 01:21:58,036
(TIRES SQUEALING)

1571
01:22:01,749 --> 01:22:04,293
- Whoa! Where'd they go?
- Where are they?

1572
01:22:04,544 --> 01:22:06,211
I don't know. She just took some guy's car.

1573
01:22:06,296 --> 01:22:07,754
- Where are they?
- That way. That way.

1574
01:22:07,839 --> 01:22:08,880
- Is that your car?
- Yeah.

1575
01:22:08,965 --> 01:22:10,424
Let's go.

1576
01:22:24,522 --> 01:22:25,647
(GRUNTS)

1577
01:22:25,815 --> 01:22:26,815
- (BRAKES SQUEAL)
- Whoa!

1578
01:22:35,950 --> 01:22:36,992
There he is!

1579
01:22:46,461 --> 01:22:48,003
(SIRENS WAILING)

1580
01:22:48,796 --> 01:22:49,796
DYLAN: Move!

1581
01:22:54,177 --> 01:22:55,218
Left!

1582
01:22:57,513 --> 01:22:59,056
We're heading east on the FDR Drive.

1583
01:22:59,265 --> 01:23:01,183
- This is not east.
- North! North!

1584
01:23:01,267 --> 01:23:03,310
- We're heading north on the FDR Drive.
- What?

1585
01:23:03,394 --> 01:23:05,479
MALE NEWSCASTER: We're coming
to you live above the FDR,

1586
01:23:05,563 --> 01:23:08,482
where NYPD and federal agents,
as you now see,

1587
01:23:08,566 --> 01:23:11,902
are engaged in a high-speed pursuit,
following a black sedan.

1588
01:23:17,033 --> 01:23:18,033
DYLAN: Fuller, where are you?

1589
01:23:18,534 --> 01:23:20,202
Right here. Trying to catch up to you now.

1590
01:23:20,370 --> 01:23:22,412
NEWSCASTER: We're now trying
to get you a better shot.

1591
01:23:24,916 --> 01:23:26,041
Come on!

1592
01:23:33,299 --> 01:23:34,341
Whoa!

1593
01:23:34,425 --> 01:23:35,425
Sorry.

1594
01:23:38,596 --> 01:23:39,596
Whoa!

1595
01:23:41,641 --> 01:23:44,851
NEWSCASTER: It looks like they're turning
onto the 59th Street Bridge.

1596
01:23:47,021 --> 01:23:51,024
As soon as we have them within range,
we will bring you those pictures live.

1597
01:23:56,072 --> 01:23:57,239
Good. Just stay with him.

1598
01:23:59,992 --> 01:24:01,326
(SIRENS WAILING)

1599
01:24:04,622 --> 01:24:05,872
Go, go, go!

1600
01:24:06,708 --> 01:24:07,749
(YELLS)

1601
01:24:09,919 --> 01:24:11,420
Behind... You're behind the bus!

1602
01:24:15,007 --> 01:24:16,091
Get over!

1603
01:24:16,843 --> 01:24:17,926
Ha-ha!

1604
01:24:19,637 --> 01:24:20,679
Oh, shit!

1605
01:24:23,141 --> 01:24:24,182
Uh-oh!

1606
01:24:44,245 --> 01:24:45,245
Come here!

1607
01:24:46,539 --> 01:24:47,956
Get back! Get back!

1608
01:24:49,417 --> 01:24:50,751
Dylan, let's go, man!

1609
01:24:50,918 --> 01:24:51,960
Come on, you...

1610
01:24:53,421 --> 01:24:55,505
FULLER: Come on, man! Get out!
DYLAN: He's gonna die in here.

1611
01:24:55,590 --> 01:24:58,925
Leave him! There's nothing you can do!
Let's go! Leave him!

1612
01:25:03,765 --> 01:25:05,140
- DYLAN: The paper!
- FULLER: Dylan!

1613
01:25:05,391 --> 01:25:07,309
Let's go! Let's go! Come on!

1614
01:25:32,627 --> 01:25:34,669
NEWSCASTER: Today,
the unfolding story of a popular

1615
01:25:34,837 --> 01:25:36,880
and controversial group of magicians,

1616
01:25:36,964 --> 01:25:38,965
who have been fast capturing
the public's imagination,

1617
01:25:39,050 --> 01:25:42,385
took a dark turn
when a police action that began in Chinatown

1618
01:25:42,470 --> 01:25:46,264
developed into a dramatic, high-speed chase
across the 59th Street Bridge,

1619
01:25:46,349 --> 01:25:49,309
which caused a fatal collision
that took the life of Jack Wilder,

1620
01:25:49,393 --> 01:25:51,686
one of the so-called Four Horsemen.

1621
01:25:52,897 --> 01:25:56,983
The whereabouts of the other three
Horsemen remain unknown at this time.

1622
01:26:01,864 --> 01:26:04,407
FULLER: Dylan, they just
figured out what the paper was in Jack's car.

1623
01:26:04,534 --> 01:26:05,700
So they know what it is?

1624
01:26:05,910 --> 01:26:07,536
And why the kid died trying to protect it.

1625
01:26:07,703 --> 01:26:09,246
Evans is on his way to brief us right now.

1626
01:26:09,455 --> 01:26:10,497
Let's go.

1627
01:26:11,082 --> 01:26:12,415
You're gonna wanna take this first, though.

1628
01:26:12,500 --> 01:26:13,458
What's that?

1629
01:26:13,543 --> 01:26:15,252
Your friend Thaddeus Bradley.

1630
01:26:16,379 --> 01:26:17,379
Rhodes.

1631
01:26:17,713 --> 01:26:19,297
You do understand the function

1632
01:26:19,382 --> 01:26:21,550
of the magician's assistant,
don't you, Agent Rhodes?

1633
01:26:21,884 --> 01:26:24,553
Yeah, she's there to distract them
while he sets up the trick.

1634
01:26:24,828 --> 01:26:25,953
I'm going to go with her.

1635
01:26:26,163 --> 01:26:27,371
Go. I got your back. I'll be right here.

1636
01:26:29,041 --> 01:26:29,915
Go ahead!

1637
01:26:30,083 --> 01:26:31,542
That's on you, Fuller.

1638
01:26:47,184 --> 01:26:51,187
Let's go, let's go! Now, now, now!

1639
01:27:02,366 --> 01:27:03,407
Daniel?

1640
01:27:03,843 --> 01:27:06,845
(CHUCKLES) You'd be right
if you weren't so wrong.

1641
01:27:07,263 --> 01:27:08,972
While you're watching the magician,

1642
01:27:09,640 --> 01:27:12,225
that lovely innocent is actually
pulling the strings.

1643
01:27:12,310 --> 01:27:15,395
Don't you find it peculiar that Interpol
would send you

1644
01:27:15,479 --> 01:27:18,982
a first timer off the desk to be your assistant?

1645
01:27:19,483 --> 01:27:21,651
Why did she request to be put on the case?

1646
01:27:21,986 --> 01:27:23,945
- She was assigned to the case.
- Oh.

1647
01:27:24,947 --> 01:27:26,323
Luck of the draw.

1648
01:27:26,782 --> 01:27:29,826
Like choosing a random card in the deck.

1649
01:27:30,036 --> 01:27:33,580
I find it odd, your sudden act of generosity.

1650
01:27:33,664 --> 01:27:34,831
What's in it for you?

1651
01:27:34,999 --> 01:27:36,833
Just trying to even the game.

1652
01:27:37,126 --> 01:27:40,962
I feel like I'm playing with somebody
wearing ankle weights and flippers.

1653
01:27:42,173 --> 01:27:45,967
Keep up, Agent Rhodes. Keep up.

1654
01:27:49,805 --> 01:27:50,847
FULLER: Hey.

1655
01:27:51,182 --> 01:27:52,390
We got a problem.

1656
01:27:53,559 --> 01:27:54,643
COWAN: Here's the safe.

1657
01:27:54,727 --> 01:27:57,520
No, no, no. Hey. What's he doing here?

1658
01:27:57,688 --> 01:27:59,147
Giving us our first solid lead.

1659
01:27:59,231 --> 01:28:02,317
We've been investigating a private security
contractor called Elkhorn

1660
01:28:02,401 --> 01:28:04,069
- for the last five years.
- And?

1661
01:28:04,153 --> 01:28:06,279
They've been hiding close
to a half billion dollars...

1662
01:28:06,364 --> 01:28:08,865
I didn't ask you. I asked him.

1663
01:28:09,241 --> 01:28:11,451
The money's in a vault inside
a warehouse in Queens.

1664
01:28:11,535 --> 01:28:14,037
We think this vault
is your magicians' final target.

1665
01:28:14,413 --> 01:28:16,122
COWAN: The magician
who died on the bridge...

1666
01:28:16,207 --> 01:28:19,834
You pulled our classified Elkhorn file
right from his crispy little hand.

1667
01:28:20,127 --> 01:28:22,462
And despite their bullshit
Robin Hood razzle-dazzle,

1668
01:28:22,546 --> 01:28:24,297
your magicians are nothing
more than common thieves.

1669
01:28:24,382 --> 01:28:25,548
How did they get the file?

1670
01:28:27,009 --> 01:28:30,011
This is the part you're gonna find
particularly interesting, Agent Rhodes.

1671
01:28:30,221 --> 01:28:34,933
They patched to my server after they accessed
your mobile command center in New Orleans

1672
01:28:35,017 --> 01:28:36,601
with codes they got from your phone.

1673
01:28:38,729 --> 01:28:40,563
You ordered us all out to chase after them.

1674
01:28:41,023 --> 01:28:43,483
The level of incompetence
displayed on this case,

1675
01:28:43,567 --> 01:28:45,568
that's a magic trick in and of itself.

1676
01:28:46,237 --> 01:28:48,530
Abracadabra. I'm taking over.

1677
01:28:49,949 --> 01:28:51,866
Boss, he's taking over?

1678
01:28:52,410 --> 01:28:53,910
EVANS: Let's go, gentlemen.

1679
01:28:55,746 --> 01:28:56,746
DYLAN: Hey.

1680
01:28:56,872 --> 01:28:58,748
Hey. I want to have a word with you.

1681
01:28:58,833 --> 01:28:59,958
Don't ever talk to me like that again.

1682
01:29:00,042 --> 01:29:02,419
- Why the hell did you take this case?
- What?

1683
01:29:02,503 --> 01:29:04,587
People say I'm "hard to read. "
That's an American expression.

1684
01:29:04,672 --> 01:29:05,922
Do you understand it?

1685
01:29:06,048 --> 01:29:07,090
Yes.

1686
01:29:07,216 --> 01:29:09,217
Good, then let me make myself
perfectly clear to you.

1687
01:29:09,427 --> 01:29:13,221
If I find out that you are anything other than
who you say you are, I swear...

1688
01:29:13,347 --> 01:29:15,056
And we French also have an expression.

1689
01:29:15,725 --> 01:29:16,850
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

1690
01:29:16,934 --> 01:29:18,518
"Faith can move mountains. "

1691
01:29:18,728 --> 01:29:22,355
If we hope to capture The Horsemen,
then you need to have a little faith in me.

1692
01:29:22,565 --> 01:29:24,566
Because I've done nothing
to deserve otherwise.

1693
01:29:24,734 --> 01:29:27,360
I just got my ass handed to me.

1694
01:29:27,445 --> 01:29:28,987
I am losing this case.

1695
01:29:29,071 --> 01:29:32,407
So faith is a luxury
I don't have any time for right now.

1696
01:29:38,622 --> 01:29:40,832
DANIEL: More than anything in his life,

1697
01:29:40,916 --> 01:29:46,337
Jack wanted to be
the most famous magician who ever lived.

1698
01:29:46,422 --> 01:29:47,797
And I can't say he achieved it,

1699
01:29:47,882 --> 01:29:51,801
but I do hope wherever he is,
it is full of magic.

1700
01:29:53,596 --> 01:29:55,930
But the point is... Sorry.

1701
01:29:56,015 --> 01:29:57,474
The point is...

1702
01:29:57,558 --> 01:30:03,772
The point of why we are here is to say
that we are not... We cannot quit now.

1703
01:30:03,856 --> 01:30:06,357
We've started something bigger than all of us.

1704
01:30:06,442 --> 01:30:08,276
We have to finish it.

1705
01:30:10,821 --> 01:30:12,489
(SIRENS WAILING)

1706
01:30:17,369 --> 01:30:18,453
MAN: Approaching the warehouse.

1707
01:30:18,621 --> 01:30:21,164
Units 5 and 6
cover the north and south entrances.

1708
01:30:21,415 --> 01:30:22,665
We are going for the vault.

1709
01:30:27,505 --> 01:30:30,423
Hey. Where's the safe? Where's the safe?

1710
01:30:34,637 --> 01:30:35,595
EVANS: What is this?

1711
01:30:35,679 --> 01:30:36,971
Where the hell is the goddamn safe?

1712
01:30:37,139 --> 01:30:38,932
We just moved it while you were outside.

1713
01:30:39,099 --> 01:30:40,266
- Evans' orders.
- COWAN: What?

1714
01:30:40,351 --> 01:30:41,392
I never said that.

1715
01:30:41,477 --> 01:30:44,437
Sir, you got a phone call
and said Washington wants the safe moved.

1716
01:30:44,647 --> 01:30:46,689
You never heard that
come out of my mouth, Agent.

1717
01:30:46,816 --> 01:30:47,315
What happened?

1718
01:30:47,483 --> 01:30:49,859
What happened? You tell me what's going on,
because this is bullshit!

1719
01:30:49,944 --> 01:30:51,319
No!

1720
01:30:53,239 --> 01:30:54,864
(CLASSICAL MUSIC PLAYING)

1721
01:30:57,201 --> 01:30:58,701
Jesus Christ.

1722
01:30:58,869 --> 01:31:01,871
Sir? Sir? What are you doing?

1723
01:31:01,956 --> 01:31:03,790
I think it's Beethoven's Concerto in D-Major.

1724
01:31:03,874 --> 01:31:06,042
- Where's the safe?
- His team is loading the truck.

1725
01:31:10,381 --> 01:31:12,048
- Hey! Hey!
- Hey!

1726
01:31:13,592 --> 01:31:14,759
- DYLAN: Stop the truck!
- Stop!

1727
01:31:15,761 --> 01:31:17,178
- Stop!
- Hey! Stop that truck!

1728
01:31:17,888 --> 01:31:19,931
(DYLAN AND FULLER CONTINUE YELLING)

1729
01:31:26,564 --> 01:31:28,439
What the hell's going on? We got our orders.

1730
01:31:28,524 --> 01:31:30,024
Now you've got new orders. Open it up.

1731
01:31:34,238 --> 01:31:35,697
Okay. Here's what I want.

1732
01:31:36,073 --> 01:31:38,366
At this moment,
they think that safe's leaving this site.

1733
01:31:38,742 --> 01:31:41,869
So we stay with it.
We follow it all the way to... Where's it going?

1734
01:31:41,954 --> 01:31:43,204
5 Pointz. Up the street.

1735
01:31:43,539 --> 01:31:46,416
So we go to 5 Pointz.
Wherever the safe goes, we go.

1736
01:31:46,584 --> 01:31:47,709
It'll lead us right to 'em.

1737
01:31:48,586 --> 01:31:49,794
You two are with me.

1738
01:32:02,558 --> 01:32:03,558
Guys...

1739
01:32:04,643 --> 01:32:07,061
Look. Office just called with this.

1740
01:32:07,146 --> 01:32:09,188
Horsemen posted it to YouTube
20 minutes ago.

1741
01:32:09,273 --> 01:32:13,234
The point of why we're here
is to say that we are not...

1742
01:32:13,319 --> 01:32:15,111
We cannot quit now.

1743
01:32:15,321 --> 01:32:19,282
We've started something bigger than all of us.
We have to finish it.

1744
01:32:19,366 --> 01:32:22,201
Remember the name Jack Wilder
when you see us live,

1745
01:32:22,286 --> 01:32:24,078
5 Pointz, Queens, 7:00.

1746
01:32:24,163 --> 01:32:26,706
Their show is in a half an hour.
It's exactly where we're headed.

1747
01:32:26,790 --> 01:32:29,208
I don't know, boss.
I don't wanna be the naysayer,

1748
01:32:29,293 --> 01:32:31,210
but these guys are kinda tricky.

1749
01:32:31,295 --> 01:32:33,921
Rhodes, they're entertainers.

1750
01:32:36,508 --> 01:32:38,676
NEWSCASTER 1: A stunning
turnout here in 5 Pointz

1751
01:32:38,761 --> 01:32:42,055
as the renegade Horsemen
taunt the FBl into a final showdown.

1752
01:32:42,139 --> 01:32:44,057
NEWSCASTER 2: The Horsemen have
invited us to their final round

1753
01:32:44,141 --> 01:32:46,309
of their three-act face-off with the FBl.

1754
01:32:46,810 --> 01:32:50,188
What do they have in store?
We're about to find out.

1755
01:32:50,314 --> 01:32:52,106
(CROWD CHEERING)

1756
01:32:52,858 --> 01:32:54,359
(SIRENS WAILING)

1757
01:33:01,533 --> 01:33:03,743
COWAN: All eyes on the truck.
Let's see who approaches.

1758
01:33:03,827 --> 01:33:04,827
Copy that.

1759
01:33:21,387 --> 01:33:23,179
FEMALE FBl AGENT: Agents Rhodes, Fuller?

1760
01:33:23,889 --> 01:33:24,889
Go, for us.

1761
01:33:25,015 --> 01:33:27,517
We've got movement.
Someone's walking toward the truck.

1762
01:33:27,726 --> 01:33:28,851
It's a woman.

1763
01:33:33,023 --> 01:33:34,399
- FULLER: Freeze!
- Oh, shit!

1764
01:33:34,483 --> 01:33:35,692
(GUNS COCKING)

1765
01:33:35,984 --> 01:33:37,485
THADDEUS: What the hell's going on?

1766
01:33:38,529 --> 01:33:40,863
COWAN: Hey! It's the guy from the TV.

1767
01:33:40,948 --> 01:33:41,989
Put your guns down.

1768
01:33:42,241 --> 01:33:44,951
Look who it is. The fifth Horseman.

1769
01:33:45,035 --> 01:33:48,246
Are you kidding?
I'm following them, just like you are.

1770
01:33:48,330 --> 01:33:51,499
I'm not following anybody anymore.
You've been ahead of us this whole time.

1771
01:33:51,583 --> 01:33:53,209
But guess what? I'm ahead of you now.

1772
01:33:53,544 --> 01:33:55,211
Your ass is mine.

1773
01:33:55,379 --> 01:33:57,046
You guys are still idiots.

1774
01:33:57,131 --> 01:33:59,382
- Yeah?
- This happens to be the former

1775
01:33:59,466 --> 01:34:01,551
rehearsal space for Lionel Shrike.

1776
01:34:02,219 --> 01:34:04,053
It's where I did my first show.

1777
01:34:04,221 --> 01:34:07,056
Now, if you wanna look
like even bigger idiots,

1778
01:34:07,224 --> 01:34:08,516
why not open it?

1779
01:34:08,892 --> 01:34:10,518
And while you're doing it, Agent Rhodes,

1780
01:34:10,936 --> 01:34:14,605
would you mind reenacting your look
of absolute befuddlement for me?

1781
01:34:14,857 --> 01:34:16,941
It will make a wonderful cover for my DVD.

1782
01:34:18,402 --> 01:34:19,402
Open the safe.

1783
01:34:19,486 --> 01:34:20,528
- Go ahead.
- DYLAN: Open it.

1784
01:34:24,533 --> 01:34:26,242
- (BEEPS)
- AGENT: What the hell?

1785
01:34:28,787 --> 01:34:29,871
What?

1786
01:34:30,122 --> 01:34:33,583
Give me that. No. No!

1787
01:34:36,879 --> 01:34:38,129
(LOCK TUMBLERS MOVING)

1788
01:34:38,255 --> 01:34:39,297
What is this?

1789
01:34:39,590 --> 01:34:41,299
- (CLUNKING)
- Get back!

1790
01:34:47,055 --> 01:34:48,431
(BALLOONS SQUEAKING)

1791
01:34:48,849 --> 01:34:50,975
Who doesn't love a good magic trick?

1792
01:34:51,769 --> 01:34:54,103
They have you chasing empty safes again.

1793
01:34:55,439 --> 01:34:58,649
Once again, misdirection.

1794
01:35:05,616 --> 01:35:07,116
The show is starting. Move out!

1795
01:35:07,326 --> 01:35:09,786
The question I'd be asking now,
Agent Rhodes is...

1796
01:35:10,287 --> 01:35:12,455
"What happened to the real one?"

1797
01:35:29,306 --> 01:35:30,515
(SIRENS BLARING)

1798
01:35:33,101 --> 01:35:34,852
COWAN: Clear! Clear 'em out!

1799
01:35:34,937 --> 01:35:36,479
Come on. Move 'em out.
Move 'em out of the way.

1800
01:35:37,940 --> 01:35:39,816
FBl! Give me a path!

1801
01:35:40,442 --> 01:35:42,026
Clear out! Clear out!

1802
01:35:42,277 --> 01:35:43,653
DANIEL: What is magic?

1803
01:35:44,488 --> 01:35:45,530
Magic is deception.

1804
01:35:45,656 --> 01:35:49,158
But deception designed to delight,
to entertain, to inspire.

1805
01:35:49,243 --> 01:35:51,702
Look out! Clear! Clear! Look out!

1806
01:35:52,162 --> 01:35:53,287
DANIEL: It is about belief.

1807
01:35:53,372 --> 01:35:54,372
MERRITT: Faith.

1808
01:35:54,498 --> 01:35:55,456
HENLEY: Trust.

1809
01:35:55,541 --> 01:35:56,666
(CROWD CHEERING)

1810
01:35:59,503 --> 01:36:00,837
Without those qualities,

1811
01:36:00,963 --> 01:36:04,382
magic, as an art form, would no longer exist.

1812
01:36:04,967 --> 01:36:09,095
HENLEY: But what happens if these qualities
are not used for their higher purpose?

1813
01:36:09,179 --> 01:36:11,848
And instead they're used to cheat, lie.

1814
01:36:11,932 --> 01:36:14,141
DANIEL: For personal gain or for greed.

1815
01:36:14,560 --> 01:36:16,310
Then it's no longer magic.

1816
01:36:16,395 --> 01:36:17,478
It's crime.

1817
01:36:17,688 --> 01:36:23,818
So tonight, for our final act,
you're gonna help us set a few things right.

1818
01:36:27,739 --> 01:36:28,906
What's going on here, Rhodes?

1819
01:36:29,157 --> 01:36:30,324
I don't know.

1820
01:36:31,368 --> 01:36:32,577
Showtime.

1821
01:36:37,708 --> 01:36:38,749
Look!

1822
01:36:43,046 --> 01:36:44,964
There they are on the roof. Let's move!

1823
01:36:45,048 --> 01:36:46,382
Go, go, go!

1824
01:36:47,092 --> 01:36:48,384
- Dylan!
- FBl, coming through!

1825
01:36:49,845 --> 01:36:50,803
What are you doing here?

1826
01:36:50,888 --> 01:36:53,431
They're going in the wrong direction
and you know it.

1827
01:36:53,765 --> 01:36:55,975
Rhodes! I need all personnel now!

1828
01:36:56,059 --> 01:36:59,395
You need to trust me. Take your leap of faith.

1829
01:37:00,355 --> 01:37:01,397
Wait.

1830
01:37:02,316 --> 01:37:03,524
- Yeah?
- Uh...

1831
01:37:03,650 --> 01:37:08,112
As our, let's call it, year of living dangerously

1832
01:37:08,196 --> 01:37:11,741
comes to a close,
in a rare moment of vulnerability,

1833
01:37:11,825 --> 01:37:16,537
I'd like to express a sentiment
to you about our relationship.

1834
01:37:16,622 --> 01:37:17,663
Okay.

1835
01:37:17,998 --> 01:37:21,500
Well, when I first met you,
I thought you were kind of a

1836
01:37:23,337 --> 01:37:25,254
- dick.
- (LAUGHS) Oh.

1837
01:37:25,339 --> 01:37:26,714
(LAUGHS) And?

1838
01:37:28,717 --> 01:37:30,384
No, that's it.

1839
01:37:30,636 --> 01:37:31,594
That's very nice.

1840
01:37:31,678 --> 01:37:33,095
- Yeah.
- I'm touched.

1841
01:37:33,180 --> 01:37:34,764
Yeah. Just from the heart.

1842
01:37:35,015 --> 01:37:36,515
Well, I didn't tell you where I was touched.

1843
01:37:36,600 --> 01:37:37,642
Oh, you!

1844
01:37:37,726 --> 01:37:38,893
(CHUCKLING)

1845
01:37:41,355 --> 01:37:43,022
Oh, God.
What are we gonna do when this is over?

1846
01:37:43,315 --> 01:37:46,150
We're on our own.
Our instructions run out after the show.

1847
01:37:47,027 --> 01:37:50,488
Even if there is no "Eye,"
if we were completely played and we spend

1848
01:37:50,572 --> 01:37:55,076
the next 20 years in jail, then,
I just want to say that...

1849
01:37:55,327 --> 01:37:57,703
I know. Me, too.

1850
01:37:58,038 --> 01:38:00,998
Whoa. (LAUGHS)
Little too sentimental for me.

1851
01:38:05,837 --> 01:38:07,338
(CHEERING)

1852
01:38:07,923 --> 01:38:09,006
There they are!

1853
01:38:12,010 --> 01:38:14,720
Go grab 'em! Put 'em down! Go, go, go!

1854
01:38:14,888 --> 01:38:15,888
Grab 'em!

1855
01:38:17,391 --> 01:38:18,432
(CROWD GROANS)

1856
01:38:19,726 --> 01:38:20,768
(CROWD LAUGHING)

1857
01:38:20,894 --> 01:38:21,936
Get up!

1858
01:38:22,396 --> 01:38:23,562
What the hell?

1859
01:38:27,359 --> 01:38:28,526
Ah, shit!

1860
01:38:29,611 --> 01:38:31,112
(PANTING)

1861
01:38:37,744 --> 01:38:39,245
- HENLEY: Hello, New York!
- (CROWD CHEERING)

1862
01:38:47,462 --> 01:38:49,338
Thank you for the magic.

1863
01:38:49,589 --> 01:38:53,801
And thank you for being such
an incredible and dedicated audience.

1864
01:38:54,219 --> 01:38:58,097
Unfortunately, like all good things,
it must come to an end.

1865
01:39:00,809 --> 01:39:02,977
So we would like to start our show tonight...

1866
01:39:03,395 --> 01:39:04,937
By saying goodbye.

1867
01:39:05,105 --> 01:39:06,188
(CHEERING)

1868
01:39:06,273 --> 01:39:09,483
HENLEY: All we wanted was to
bring the world to a magic show.

1869
01:39:09,568 --> 01:39:12,111
DANIEL: And thereby bring a little magic
back to the world.

1870
01:39:16,491 --> 01:39:17,616
DYLAN: Clear the way!

1871
01:39:27,419 --> 01:39:30,629
MERRITT: This has been
one hell of a ride for all of us.

1872
01:39:31,131 --> 01:39:33,466
But it's time for us to disappear.

1873
01:39:33,675 --> 01:39:35,009
DANIEL: Good night, New York.

1874
01:39:35,260 --> 01:39:36,635
MERRITT: And thank you for believing in us.

1875
01:39:39,306 --> 01:39:40,473
DYLAN: Stop!

1876
01:39:43,977 --> 01:39:44,977
Freeze!

1877
01:39:45,812 --> 01:39:47,021
- No!
- (GUNSHOT)

1878
01:40:04,664 --> 01:40:05,956
God damn it!

1879
01:40:34,569 --> 01:40:35,778
I'm sorry.

1880
01:40:36,404 --> 01:40:38,531
You were right. It's bigger than all of us.

1881
01:40:39,533 --> 01:40:43,619
This is one time I'm not happy being right.

1882
01:40:45,914 --> 01:40:47,665
So I guess this is it.

1883
01:40:49,584 --> 01:40:50,751
Is it?

1884
01:41:16,736 --> 01:41:18,028
Dylan!

1885
01:41:18,446 --> 01:41:20,698
Dylan! Dylan!

1886
01:41:20,991 --> 01:41:22,032
Hey.

1887
01:41:23,451 --> 01:41:25,369
- You see that?
- What?

1888
01:41:29,040 --> 01:41:30,416
Where's the real money?

1889
01:41:37,007 --> 01:41:38,132
(CAR ALARM BLARING)

1890
01:41:46,641 --> 01:41:50,603
MAN: You're under arrest!
Hands in the air! Now!

1891
01:41:54,649 --> 01:41:57,860
I want two each inside of here.
The other 30 around here.

1892
01:41:57,986 --> 01:41:59,361
Roofs, alleys, balconies.

1893
01:41:59,446 --> 01:42:02,531
- Eyes on The Horsemen at all times.
- Yes, sir.

1894
01:42:02,616 --> 01:42:06,452
Wow, 100 years ago, William Robinson
took the name Chung Ling Soo

1895
01:42:06,536 --> 01:42:10,414
and spent his entire life
never speaking English in public.

1896
01:42:10,624 --> 01:42:11,832
(SPEAKS FRENCH)

1897
01:42:12,209 --> 01:42:14,043
This other guy, Maximillian...

1898
01:42:14,252 --> 01:42:17,254
I am not interested
in a history lesson on magic at this moment.

1899
01:43:06,262 --> 01:43:07,388
I've been framed.

1900
01:43:08,723 --> 01:43:11,266
- I'm sure you were.
- Yeah, but I can prove it.

1901
01:43:11,601 --> 01:43:12,893
I always do.

1902
01:43:13,269 --> 01:43:15,229
Just like I predicted that you'd play the fool.

1903
01:43:15,313 --> 01:43:17,815
Let's just drop the theatricality, all right?

1904
01:43:18,066 --> 01:43:20,234
The cameras aren't rolling in here.

1905
01:43:20,443 --> 01:43:22,903
Fellas, can I have a few minutes
with my friend here alone, please.

1906
01:43:22,988 --> 01:43:24,113
GUARD: Sure.

1907
01:43:29,828 --> 01:43:30,869
THADDEUS: All right.

1908
01:43:31,913 --> 01:43:33,539
- I got information to trade.
- Mmm.

1909
01:43:33,623 --> 01:43:34,748
I believe that's how it's done. Huh?

1910
01:43:34,833 --> 01:43:36,458
If it's of some value.

1911
01:43:39,129 --> 01:43:42,297
These bars give a man time to think.

1912
01:43:43,466 --> 01:43:46,760
And I'm pretty sure I know how they did it.

1913
01:43:47,429 --> 01:43:49,513
Remember the rabbit trick
in the second show?

1914
01:43:50,473 --> 01:43:52,307
The box was never empty.

1915
01:43:53,393 --> 01:43:54,560
(WHIRRING)

1916
01:43:54,686 --> 01:43:55,853
The room wasn't either.

1917
01:43:57,272 --> 01:43:59,648
After gaining access to the warehouse,

1918
01:43:59,858 --> 01:44:01,942
The Horsemen left the real safe

1919
01:44:02,027 --> 01:44:06,989
and transformed the whole room
into a giant rabbit box.

1920
01:44:08,616 --> 01:44:13,454
You go charging in there,
thinking the safe was already gone.

1921
01:44:13,663 --> 01:44:14,663
Hey!

1922
01:44:14,748 --> 01:44:16,040
Hey! Stop!

1923
01:44:16,249 --> 01:44:17,499
Missing the trick. Again.

1924
01:44:17,584 --> 01:44:20,753
Which was to make you think
the safe had already been stolen,

1925
01:44:20,837 --> 01:44:22,921
so you'd drop your guard and leave.

1926
01:44:23,465 --> 01:44:26,425
Now, while you were busy
playing with balloon animals,

1927
01:44:26,634 --> 01:44:29,219
someone was breaking into the warehouse.

1928
01:44:47,739 --> 01:44:48,906
Who?

1929
01:44:50,325 --> 01:44:51,825
Jack Wilder.

1930
01:44:52,577 --> 01:44:53,911
Holy shit.

1931
01:44:54,120 --> 01:44:56,497
No. No way. He died right in front of my eyes.

1932
01:44:57,290 --> 01:44:59,374
Unless, of course, he didn't.

1933
01:45:06,716 --> 01:45:08,008
It's locked.

1934
01:45:08,802 --> 01:45:10,010
JACK: Weren't you listening?

1935
01:45:10,512 --> 01:45:11,553
Nothing's ever locked.

1936
01:45:11,721 --> 01:45:12,805
MERRITT: Ah!

1937
01:45:12,972 --> 01:45:15,557
Well done, Mr. Wilder! Good work.

1938
01:45:15,642 --> 01:45:17,601
MERRITT: You're a big boy now, Jack.

1939
01:45:17,685 --> 01:45:20,062
He escaped in a standard FBl vehicle, right?

1940
01:45:24,109 --> 01:45:25,442
Led you to the bridge.

1941
01:45:25,693 --> 01:45:29,321
Where the other Horsemen were waiting
with an identical replacement car.

1942
01:45:30,323 --> 01:45:32,407
It only took a split second
for you to lose contact with it

1943
01:45:32,492 --> 01:45:33,492
and make the switch.

1944
01:45:43,419 --> 01:45:44,503
(MERRITT LAUGHS)

1945
01:45:46,756 --> 01:45:48,173
- Oh!
- (LAUGHS)

1946
01:45:55,807 --> 01:45:58,809
THADDEUS: When you crawled
into that burning car,

1947
01:45:59,185 --> 01:46:01,186
quite heroically, I might add,

1948
01:46:03,064 --> 01:46:05,149
you almost died trying to rescue

1949
01:46:05,233 --> 01:46:08,235
what I assume was a cadaver
from the morgue.

1950
01:46:09,737 --> 01:46:13,407
DYLAN: Why go through such an elaborate
and dangerous plan

1951
01:46:14,284 --> 01:46:16,493
- just to frame one guy?
- I don't know.

1952
01:46:16,578 --> 01:46:18,579
They never kept any of the money they took.

1953
01:46:18,663 --> 01:46:21,039
Yeah, that's the part
I haven't been able to put together yet.

1954
01:46:21,124 --> 01:46:23,709
But I just gave you information that
is substantially more important.

1955
01:46:23,793 --> 01:46:25,669
- No. Not really.
- What?

1956
01:46:25,753 --> 01:46:30,090
I finally got a chance to really look into
Lionel Shrike.

1957
01:46:30,508 --> 01:46:33,343
His comeback attempt. His accident.

1958
01:46:34,304 --> 01:46:37,806
The insurer who denied the family's claim?

1959
01:46:38,057 --> 01:46:39,266
Tressler Insurance.

1960
01:46:41,186 --> 01:46:43,437
The bank that carried the note?

1961
01:46:44,480 --> 01:46:46,064
Credit Republican of Paris.

1962
01:46:46,149 --> 01:46:47,733
Credit Republicain de Paris.

1963
01:46:49,360 --> 01:46:50,652
DYLAN: What do you make of that?

1964
01:46:50,862 --> 01:46:52,821
A sucker is born every minute.

1965
01:46:53,781 --> 01:46:59,036
What if all this was just leading up to us
getting mugged in Central Park at 2:00 a. m.?

1966
01:46:59,120 --> 01:47:01,288
No, I'm telling you,
we're right where we need to be.

1967
01:47:02,040 --> 01:47:04,291
- We just have to find...
- That?

1968
01:47:06,836 --> 01:47:08,587
DANIEL: The Lionel Shrike tree.

1969
01:47:09,339 --> 01:47:11,340
HENLEY: And the card encased in glass.

1970
01:47:13,384 --> 01:47:14,843
What do we do now?

1971
01:47:31,653 --> 01:47:33,111
Oh, nice!

1972
01:47:34,906 --> 01:47:37,074
(CAROUSEL MUSIC PLAYING)

1973
01:47:49,087 --> 01:47:50,545
DYLAN: So, here's my new theory.

1974
01:47:50,880 --> 01:47:54,341
The legend is that the "Eye" is everywhere.

1975
01:47:55,009 --> 01:47:56,176
Waiting

1976
01:47:56,552 --> 01:48:00,347
for the truly great magicians
to distinguish themselves

1977
01:48:01,307 --> 01:48:03,058
from the mediocre ones.

1978
01:48:03,810 --> 01:48:05,060
Maybe that was you.

1979
01:48:05,770 --> 01:48:08,021
Deep down inside you wanted nothing more

1980
01:48:08,106 --> 01:48:10,482
than to be part of the "Eye,"
but you were never invited.

1981
01:48:10,817 --> 01:48:13,902
So you try to destroy them.
But instead what happens?

1982
01:48:14,445 --> 01:48:15,904
You pissed them off.

1983
01:48:17,657 --> 01:48:20,659
The Eye isn't real.

1984
01:48:20,743 --> 01:48:23,829
Okay, then, explain then.
Who's behind all this.

1985
01:48:24,289 --> 01:48:25,872
Somebody with an obsession.

1986
01:48:25,957 --> 01:48:27,124
- Meticulous.
- Who?

1987
01:48:27,208 --> 01:48:30,377
Somebody prepared to sacrifice everything.

1988
01:48:30,461 --> 01:48:34,673
Somebody so prepared to lose
that they wouldn't even be a suspect

1989
01:48:34,757 --> 01:48:35,799
until the trick was done.

1990
01:48:35,883 --> 01:48:38,593
I don't want a profile. I need a name.
Who? Who?

1991
01:48:38,678 --> 01:48:40,387
I don't know who.

1992
01:48:40,847 --> 01:48:44,349
But they had to have access to the warehouse
to plant the mirrors.

1993
01:48:45,768 --> 01:48:49,688
Always a step ahead of me. And the FBl.

1994
01:48:49,772 --> 01:48:53,025
Got past them not once,
not twice, but consistently.

1995
01:48:53,443 --> 01:48:55,444
Almost as if they were on the in...

1996
01:49:08,833 --> 01:49:10,042
DYLAN: (WHISPERING) The inside.

1997
01:49:22,347 --> 01:49:24,723
- You.
- Mmm.

1998
01:49:27,977 --> 01:49:29,144
Why?

1999
01:49:29,812 --> 01:49:31,938
That is the question, isn't it?

2000
01:49:32,982 --> 01:49:34,066
You're right.

2001
01:49:35,151 --> 01:49:39,571
I can't tell you how long I've waited
to see the look on your face.

2002
01:49:42,033 --> 01:49:43,367
Who are you?

2003
01:49:44,619 --> 01:49:45,994
What do you want from me?

2004
01:49:46,871 --> 01:49:48,372
What do I want?

2005
01:49:48,790 --> 01:49:51,708
I want you to spend
the rest of your life in this cell,

2006
01:49:51,793 --> 01:49:55,796
staring at four walls
and wondering how you missed it.

2007
01:49:56,506 --> 01:49:59,591
How you let yourself
be so blinded by your ego

2008
01:50:00,134 --> 01:50:02,552
that you convinced yourself
that you were one step ahead

2009
01:50:02,637 --> 01:50:04,971
when you were always two steps behind.

2010
01:50:10,019 --> 01:50:11,144
Dylan?

2011
01:50:12,230 --> 01:50:13,230
Wait a minute.

2012
01:50:14,273 --> 01:50:16,191
Dylan! How did this happen?

2013
01:50:18,986 --> 01:50:19,986
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

2014
01:50:21,697 --> 01:50:22,906
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

2015
01:50:24,075 --> 01:50:25,742
Dylan!

2016
01:50:25,910 --> 01:50:26,910
Why?

2017
01:50:27,370 --> 01:50:28,370
Why?

2018
01:50:32,667 --> 01:50:34,751
- MERRITT: Oh, my God.
- (JACK CHUCKLING)

2019
01:50:35,795 --> 01:50:38,964
I did not see that coming. That's impossible!

2020
01:50:39,048 --> 01:50:40,090
JACK: No way.

2021
01:50:40,174 --> 01:50:42,592
That was actually pretty good.

2022
01:50:43,010 --> 01:50:44,052
Thank you.

2023
01:50:44,512 --> 01:50:46,805
When I said,
"Always be the smartest guy in the room. "

2024
01:50:46,889 --> 01:50:47,848
We were in agreement.

2025
01:50:47,932 --> 01:50:48,974
Okay. Right.

2026
01:50:49,642 --> 01:50:50,642
Henley.

2027
01:50:51,394 --> 01:50:53,103
I've never seen her speechless.

2028
01:50:53,229 --> 01:50:54,938
I take that as a huge compliment.

2029
01:50:55,648 --> 01:50:58,316
Hey, man, I'm so sorry for kicking your ass.
Really.

2030
01:50:59,152 --> 01:51:04,364
Hey, listen, for the record,
I have always been a 100% believer.

2031
01:51:04,449 --> 01:51:07,701
And the amount of energy I have expended
to keep these infidels on point...

2032
01:51:07,785 --> 01:51:08,910
(HENLEY LAUGHING)

2033
01:51:08,995 --> 01:51:11,037
Merritt, you're in.

2034
01:51:11,873 --> 01:51:12,914
God bless.

2035
01:51:13,040 --> 01:51:14,082
DYLAN: Come.

2036
01:51:15,126 --> 01:51:20,213
The real magic is taking four strong solo acts
and making them all work together.

2037
01:51:20,298 --> 01:51:22,466
And that's exactly what you did.

2038
01:51:23,885 --> 01:51:24,926
So welcome.

2039
01:51:28,264 --> 01:51:30,348
Welcome to the Eye.

2040
01:51:32,643 --> 01:51:33,768
(HENLEY GASPS)

2041
01:52:37,500 --> 01:52:39,000
It was all connected.

2042
01:52:40,253 --> 01:52:43,255
Credit Republican. Tressler Insurance.

2043
01:52:45,424 --> 01:52:46,550
Bonjour.

2044
01:52:48,261 --> 01:52:49,511
Bonjour.

2045
01:52:52,640 --> 01:52:55,976
And Elkhorn?
What's the connection to Shrike?

2046
01:52:58,563 --> 01:53:04,109
Elkhorn started as a safe manufacturer.
They used cheap steel.

2047
01:53:05,695 --> 01:53:06,736
They cut corners.

2048
01:53:07,071 --> 01:53:10,198
When he got to the bottom of the river,
the safe warped.

2049
01:53:10,283 --> 01:53:11,658
And he was trapped.

2050
01:53:13,286 --> 01:53:14,911
He was your father.

2051
01:53:16,831 --> 01:53:20,166
DYLAN: The morning before the show
didn't feel like any other day.

2052
01:53:21,210 --> 01:53:26,214
When my father said he had to go to work,
he could see that I didn't want him to leave.

2053
01:53:28,509 --> 01:53:33,638
So he gave me his watch, and he told me
to count the seconds until he came back.

2054
01:53:34,807 --> 01:53:37,475
I have never let his watch stop since then.

2055
01:53:37,560 --> 01:53:39,686
And from that moment on,

2056
01:53:39,770 --> 01:53:42,355
I created a persona.

2057
01:53:42,982 --> 01:53:44,858
I planned. I worked out every detail.

2058
01:53:44,942 --> 01:53:48,236
But the one thing
that I couldn't imagine happening

2059
01:53:48,696 --> 01:53:49,863
was you.

2060
01:53:51,532 --> 01:53:54,492
And I know that the logical conclusion for you

2061
01:53:54,994 --> 01:53:57,704
is to take this case to its resolution.

2062
01:53:57,788 --> 01:54:00,874
And for you to turn me in.

2063
01:54:05,963 --> 01:54:07,047
Yeah.

2064
01:54:09,008 --> 01:54:12,844
But you know how I feel
about resolution and logic.

2065
01:54:14,221 --> 01:54:15,555
And you also know

2066
01:54:16,390 --> 01:54:20,727
that I think some things
are best left unexplained.

2067
01:54:27,234 --> 01:54:28,943
DYLAN: One more secret to lock away.

2068
01:54:41,082 --> 01:54:42,082
Come here!

2069
01:54:43,376 --> 01:54:44,793
Get back! Get back!

2070
01:54:46,253 --> 01:54:47,587
Dylan, let's go, man!

2071
01:54:47,755 --> 01:54:48,797
Come on, you...

2072
01:54:50,257 --> 01:54:52,342
FULLER: Come on, man! Get out!
DYLAN: He's gonna die in here.

2073
01:54:52,426 --> 01:54:55,762
Leave him! There's nothing you can do!
Let's go! Leave him!

2074
01:55:00,601 --> 01:55:01,976
- DYLAN: The paper!
- FULLER: Dylan!

2075
01:55:02,228 --> 01:55:04,145
Let's go! Let's go! Come on!

2076
01:56:53,088 --> 01:56:54,964
DANIEL: Please, stop, stop, stop.

2077
01:56:55,382 --> 01:56:59,052
All right, stop the van. Stop the van.
I'm gonna jump out of the van.

2078
01:57:00,054 --> 01:57:01,554
Oh, thank God.

2079
01:57:03,474 --> 01:57:05,558
HENLEY: Where are we?

2080
01:57:05,643 --> 01:57:08,061
Great, another shit hole.

2081
01:57:08,145 --> 01:57:10,104
Okay, feeling it.

2082
01:57:10,189 --> 01:57:14,359
I'm exhausted, and hungry, and cranky.

2083
01:57:15,402 --> 01:57:17,237
HENLEY: Check out this place.

2084
01:57:17,321 --> 01:57:18,655
MERRITT: Where'd you bring us?

2085
01:57:18,781 --> 01:57:20,156
DANIEL: Was there no landfill where we were?

2086
01:57:20,241 --> 01:57:22,075
JACK: This place is awesome.

2087
01:57:23,619 --> 01:57:25,328
- Is this our new gear?
- DANIEL: There'd better not be, like,

2088
01:57:25,412 --> 01:57:27,372
matching jumpsuits in there.
You know I don't wear spandex.

2089
01:57:27,456 --> 01:57:28,581
It's locked.

2090
01:57:28,749 --> 01:57:29,833
Guys, the cards.

2091
01:57:29,917 --> 01:57:31,125
What card?

2092
01:57:31,252 --> 01:57:32,460
DANIEL: What do you mean, "what card"?

2093
01:57:34,547 --> 01:57:35,547
Hmm.

2094
01:57:36,590 --> 01:57:37,590
Okay.

2095
01:57:37,883 --> 01:57:39,717
(UPBEAT SONG PLAYING)

2096
02:01:29,573 --> 02:01:31,324
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)